---
import SiteLayout from "../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
---
<SiteLayout
  title="DJ software features — Dubplate"
  description="Browse and analyse your DJ library, rehearse transitions, record your mix, and prepare and import classic CDJ USBs with Dubplate."
>
  <Fragment slot="head">
    <link rel="stylesheet" href={import.meta.env.BASE_URL + "features.css"}>
    <script is:inline src={import.meta.env.BASE_URL + "atlas.js"} defer></script>
  </Fragment>
  <section class="hero" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
    <h1 id="hero-title">Shape your<br><em>next set.</em></h1>
    <div class="intro">
      <p>Dig through your collection, rehearse the handoffs, then record your mix or take the set to the booth. Dubplate is free DJ software.</p>
      <a class="text-link" href="#chart">Explore the example set <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <nav class="feature-nav" aria-label="On this page">
    <ul>
      <li><a href="#library">Library</a></li>
      <li><a href="#analysis">Beat grids</a></li>
      <li><a href="#rehearse">Rehearsal</a></li>
      <li><a href="#check">Set checks</a></li>
      <li><a href="#record">Recording</a></li>
      <li><a href="#usb">USB</a></li>
    </ul>
  </nav>

  <figure class="atlas" id="chart" aria-labelledby="atlas-title" tabindex="-1">
    <div class="sheet">
      <div class="sheet-head">
        <strong id="atlas-title">Afterhours <span aria-hidden="true">/</span> Set atlas</strong>
        <span class="technical">Example running order</span>
      </div>
      <div class="map-layout">
        <div class="energy-axis technical" aria-hidden="true">
          <span>Stronger <span class="axis-arrow">↑</span></span>
          <span>Gentler</span>
        </div>
        <svg class="map" viewBox="0 0 1080 230" preserveAspectRatio="none" role="img" aria-labelledby="map-title map-description">
          <title id="map-title">Energy over the course of an example set</title>
          <desc id="map-description">The set starts gently, climbs to a strong midpoint, and eases off toward the finish.</desc>
          <defs>
            <pattern id="map-grid" width="43" height="23" patternUnits="userSpaceOnUse">
              <path d="M43 0H0V23" fill="none" stroke="#95b9a2" stroke-opacity=".24"/>
            </pattern>
          </defs>
          <rect width="1080" height="230" fill="url(#map-grid)"/>
          <g id="contours" fill="none">
            <path d="M0 155 C120 150 170 175 260 156 S430 146 500 93 S590 42 650 61 S740 119 810 130 S980 142 1080 151" stroke="#edff99" stroke-width="3"/>
          </g>
          <g id="marker" transform="translate(190 0)" aria-hidden="true">
            <path d="M0 14V214" stroke="#ecffac" stroke-dasharray="4 6" vector-effect="non-scaling-stroke"/>
          </g>
        </svg>
        <span class="map-marker" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <div class="time-axis technical" aria-hidden="true">
          <span>Start</span><span>Set progression <span class="axis-arrow">→</span></span><span>Finish</span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="tracks" role="group" aria-label="Choose a point in the example set" hidden>
        <button type="button" aria-pressed="true" aria-controls="atlas-note">Opening <span>118 BPM · 8A</span></button>
        <button type="button" aria-pressed="false" aria-controls="atlas-note">Peak <span>124 BPM · 9A</span></button>
        <button type="button" aria-pressed="false" aria-controls="atlas-note">Release <span>122 BPM · 9A</span></button>
      </div>
      <noscript><p class="technical static-tracks">Opening · 118 BPM · 8A &nbsp; / &nbsp; Peak · 124 BPM · 9A &nbsp; / &nbsp; Release · 122 BPM · 9A</p></noscript>
    </div>
    <figcaption class="annotation" id="atlas-note" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true">
      <strong id="atlas-note-title">Open the floor.</strong>
      <span id="atlas-note-text">Start with space. Mark the mix-out cue on the opener so you can rehearse the handoff in headphones.</span>
    </figcaption>
  </figure>

  <section class="feature" id="library" aria-labelledby="library-title" tabindex="-1">
    <div class="feature-copy">
      <h2 id="library-title">Find the next record.</h2>
      <p>Add music folders and browse their subfolders, or import your rekordbox collection with playlists, cues and beat grids. Copy a rekordbox playlist into Dubplate to make an editable version.</p>
      <p>Build your own playlists, group them in folders, and rate, colour or tag tracks. Select a music folder to scope your search to it and the folders inside it.</p>
      <a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/lvndry/dubplate/blob/main/docs/guide.md#dig-through-the-library">See the library filters <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
    </div>

    <figure class="check-card">
      <figcaption>
        <strong>Looking for a track</strong>
        <span class="technical">Example searches</span>
      </figcaption>
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr><th scope="col">Search</th><th scope="col">Find</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><th scope="row"><code>amapiano warmup</code></th><td>Tracks in your amapiano/warmup folder</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row"><code>bpm:120-124</code> <code>key:fits</code></th><td>Tracks in range that fit the reference key</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row"><code>tag:peak</code> <code>played:no</code></th><td>Your peak-time picks that haven’t had a full minute on a deck this session</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </figure>
  </section>

  <section class="feature readiness" id="analysis" aria-labelledby="analysis-title" tabindex="-1">
    <div class="feature-copy">
      <h2 id="analysis-title">Put beat one in place.</h2>
      <p>Dubplate analyses tracks in the background for energy on a scale of 1 to 10. For tracks without rekordbox analysis, it also detects BPM, key and the beat grid.</p>
      <p>If an amapiano track’s first downbeat lands one beat late, move it back a beat. If the grid lines sit just behind the kicks, nudge them earlier in 5&nbsp;ms steps and confirm the grid. The fix follows the track into sync and export.</p>
      <a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/lvndry/dubplate/blob/main/docs/guide.md#check-each-track">See the beat grid controls <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
    </div>

    <figure class="check-card">
      <figcaption>
        <strong>Beat grid controls</strong>
        <span class="technical">Track check</span>
      </figcaption>
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr><th scope="col">Action</th><th scope="col">Keys</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><th scope="row">Move the downbeat one beat</th><td><kbd>,</kbd> or <kbd>.</kbd></td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Nudge the grid 5&nbsp;ms</th><td><kbd>[</kbd> or <kbd>]</kbd></td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Confirm the grid</th><td><kbd>G</kbd></td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </figure>
  </section>

  <section class="feature rehearsal" id="rehearse" aria-labelledby="rehearse-title" tabindex="-1">
    <div class="feature-copy">
      <h2 id="rehearse-title">Hear the handoff.</h2>
      <p>Build a running order and keep alternatives as backups. The Next panel suggests tracks after the one you select and shows how the key, tempo and energy would change.</p>
      <p>Mark the mix-in and mix-out cues with <kbd>I</kbd> and <kbd>O</kbd>, then press <kbd>S</kbd> for a 20-second preview in your headphones. Mark a transition Free to leave it open for the room and turn off warnings for that handoff.</p>
      <a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/lvndry/dubplate/blob/main/docs/guide.md#check-each-track">Read about transition preview <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
    </div>

    <figure class="transition">
      <figcaption>
        <strong>Transition preview</strong>
        <span class="technical">Example · 20 seconds</span>
      </figcaption>
      <div class="wave-panel" aria-hidden="true">
        <div class="wave-label wave-label-out technical">Mix out</div>
        <span class="wave-cue"></span>
        <svg class="wave wave-out" viewBox="0 0 520 58" preserveAspectRatio="none">
          <path d="M0 29 7 15 14 45 21 8 28 51 35 18 42 36 49 9 56 53 63 15 70 44 77 12 84 47 91 20 98 33 105 5 112 48 119 15 126 39 133 12 140 45 147 9 154 47 161 22 168 36 175 5 182 51 189 16 196 43 203 21 210 35 217 8 224 49 231 12 238 52 245 23 252 38 259 9 266 46 273 20 280 41 287 13 294 44 301 20 308 35 315 13 322 41 329 17 336 37 343 23 350 34 357 16 364 40 371 24 378 35 385 21 392 33 399 24 406 32 413 22 420 35 427 25 434 33 441 27 448 30 455 26 462 31 469 28 476 30 483 28 490 30 520 29" />
        </svg>
        <svg class="wave wave-in" viewBox="0 0 520 58" preserveAspectRatio="none">
          <path d="M0 29 34 29 41 27 48 31 55 25 62 32 69 28 76 31 83 25 90 32 97 24 104 35 111 23 118 36 125 18 132 40 139 25 146 33 153 18 160 39 167 14 174 42 181 23 188 37 195 11 202 47 209 16 216 47 223 20 230 40 237 9 244 51 251 16 258 42 265 5 272 51 279 22 286 41 293 11 300 46 307 8 314 52 321 19 328 39 335 10 342 49 349 17 356 44 363 5 370 53 377 18 384 41 391 14 398 44 405 19 412 37 419 7 426 51 433 11 440 46 447 21 454 36 461 8 468 50 475 19 482 40 489 13 496 48 503 22 510 38 520 29" />
        </svg>
        <div class="wave-label wave-label-in technical">Mix in</div>
      </div>
      <div class="transition-meta">
        <span><strong>118 → 124</strong> BPM</span>
        <span><strong>8A → 9A</strong> Key</span>
      </div>
    </figure>
  </section>

  <section class="feature readiness" id="check" aria-labelledby="check-title" tabindex="-1">
    <div class="feature-copy">
      <h2 id="check-title">Check the set.</h2>
      <p>Dubplate flags missing files, unconfirmed beat grids, and missing mix-in or mix-out cues. When a track has phrase data, Dubplate can propose cues for you to review.</p>
      <p>Look for warnings between tracks too. If two vocals are about to overlap, try a different cue or use stems to mute the outgoing vocal.</p>
      <a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/lvndry/dubplate/blob/main/docs/guide.md#3-prepare-the-set">Read the preparation guide <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
    </div>

    <figure class="check-card">
      <figcaption>
        <strong>Track readiness</strong>
        <span class="technical">Example set</span>
      </figcaption>
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr><th scope="col">Track</th><th scope="col">Status</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><th scope="row">Opening</th><td><span class="status ready"><span aria-hidden="true">✓</span> Ready</span></td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Peak</th><td><span class="status"><span aria-hidden="true">↳</span> Mix-out cue missing</span></td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Release</th><td><span class="status"><span aria-hidden="true">↳</span> Grid unconfirmed</span></td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </figure>
  </section>

  <section class="feature" id="record" aria-labelledby="record-title" tabindex="-1">
    <div class="feature-copy">
      <h2 id="record-title">Listen back to your mix.</h2>
      <p>Click <strong>REC</strong> or press <kbd>⌘⇧R</kbd> to capture the master output as a 24-bit WAV. Dubplate saves it in <strong>Music/Dubplate Recordings</strong>.</p>
      <p>Record a practice run and listen back to the bass swap on the way into the peak track. To share what you played, export a timestamped TXT or CSV tracklist from your Dubplate session history.</p>
      <a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/lvndry/dubplate/blob/main/docs/guide.md#5-record">Read the recording guide <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
    </div>

    <figure class="check-card">
      <figcaption>
        <strong>Afterhours tracklist</strong>
        <span class="technical">Example session history</span>
      </figcaption>
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr><th scope="col">Track</th><th scope="col">Time into the set</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><th scope="row">Opening</th><td><time datetime="PT0S">00:00</time></td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Peak</th><td><time datetime="PT5M48S">05:48</time></td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Release</th><td><time datetime="PT11M26S">11:26</time></td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </figure>
  </section>

  <section class="feature readiness" id="usb" aria-labelledby="usb-title" tabindex="-1">
    <div class="feature-copy">
      <h2 id="usb-title">Take it to the booth.</h2>
      <p>Export a set, playlist or music folder with <strong>USB…</strong> for players that read classic Device Library, such as a CDJ-3000 or XDJ-RX3. The export copies the audio, track order, grids, cues, loops and waveforms. Set backups go in their own playlist.</p>
      <p>Use a fresh stick or one Dubplate previously exported. For a player that requires OneLibrary, export rekordbox XML from Dubplate, import it into rekordbox 7, and export the USB there. Direct export refuses sticks that contain OneLibrary.</p>
      <p>After playing, use <strong>Import from USB…</strong> in Library settings to read a classic Device Library stick. Bring back the CDJ’s track order and choose which cue changes to keep. The imported history contains track order only, and the stick stays read-only.</p>
      <a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/lvndry/dubplate/blob/main/docs/guide.md#play-the-set-on-cdjs">Read the USB export and import guide <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
    </div>

    <figure class="check-card">
      <figcaption>
        <strong>Choose your USB workflow</strong>
      </figcaption>
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr><th scope="col">Device library</th><th scope="col">Export from</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><th scope="row">Classic Device Library</th><td>Dubplate</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">OneLibrary</th><td>rekordbox 7</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <a class="text-link" href="https://rekordbox.com/en/support/usb-export/">Check your player’s USB format <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
    </figure>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>
